  "claims": [
    {
      "claim": "Representative L1 gold-context records report absolute or qualitative oral bioavailability at or above the 20% threshold (asciminib ~73% C10; levofloxacin ~100% C15; ofloxacin ~100% C08; CCT251921 ~70% C04; LY2196044 45% C09; vardenafil 34% C07; zidovudine 61% C03; pradigastat ~40% C02 and completely bioavailable at 10 mg C11/C13; antofloxacin high C12/C17), and no L1 record affirmatively supports F <20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C10","C15","C08","C04","C09","C07","C03","C02","C11","C13","C12","C17"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L2 absolute F measurements and related records from the same contexts are also at or above 20% (asciminib mouse 53% C31; compound 109 rat 57% C21, dog 68% C33, mouse 30% C35; LY2196044 dog 41.3% C24, rat 73.5% C28; ofloxacin virtually 100% C25; doxifluridine 55-76% C27/C32/C36/C37/C40/C42 and 34-80% ranges C19/C20/C30/C34; antofloxacin AUC ratio ~1.1 C29), with qualitative 'orally bioavailable' descriptions (C22/C23/C26/C38/C39/C41), reinforcing the high-F pattern.",
      "card_ids": ["C31","C21","C33","C35","C24","C28","C25","C27","C32","C36","C37","C40","C42","C19","C20","C30","C34","C29","C22","C23","C26","C38","C39","C41"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for the phosphate prodrug fostamatinib show substantial systemic exposure of its active moiety R406 after oral dosing (Cmax 573 ng/mL after 150 mg C63; 325 ng/mL after 80 mg C50), and capecitabine metabolite 5'-DFCR Cmax after oral prodrug dosing (C86/C55) further illustrates oral prodrug conversion; this supports the plausibility of oral absorption of the query's phosphate prodrug.",
      "card_ids": ["C63","C50","C86","C55"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L3 oral exposure records for oxazolidinones (linezolid Cmax 10.4 µg/mL after 500 mg C72 and 18.9 µg/mL at 600 mg daily C92; compound 7 Cmax 8.07 µg/mL after 300 mg C47) show that the oxazolidinone class to which the query belongs can achieve meaningful oral exposure.",
      "card_ids": ["C72","C92","C47"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "The query's charged phosphate and low logD are physicochemical liabilities, not affirmative low-F evidence; the prodrug hydrolysis pathway is supported by the fostamatinib phosphate prodrug exposure records, so the high prediction is retained.",
      "card_ids": ["C63","C50"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "oral_auc_cmax_exposure",
      "applicability": "moderate",
      "direction": "supportive",
      "decision_effect": "strengthened",
      "card_ids": ["C63","C50","C86","C55","C72","C92","C47"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule (tedizolid phosphate) or its active moiety tedizolid is present in the supplied records.",
    "L3 records provide Cmax/AUC values but not F values, so they cannot independently establish the F>=20% threshold.",
    "The extent of intestinal/plasma phosphatase conversion of the phosphate prodrug to the permeable tedizolid is not directly measured in the cards.",
    "Transferability of the high-F contexts and L3 exposure records to the query is inferred from class/prodrug similarity rather than directly demonstrated.",
    "No query-specific permeability, solubility, or first-pass data are supplied."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "All L1/L2 gold-context records report F >=20% with no affirmative low-F evidence, and L3 oral exposure records for the phosphate prodrug fostamatinib and for oxazolidinones support the plausibility of oral absorption despite the query's charged phosphate; the low physicochemical prior is not endpoint proof, so the prediction remains high with moderate confidence."
}

